                        "glosses": [
                            "The flat upper part of a ship's stern above the transom, often decorated with carvings."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bc921ae0-58b6-3bb2-9da9-4ca8d842f0c3",
                        "entry_id": "f464fd8f-2fca-375a-9474-c0383ed70bd6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The taffrail."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7462215a-61a7-431b-9625-eee85906c7c1",
                                "sense_id": "bc921ae0-58b6-3bb2-9da9-4ca8d842f0c3",
                                "text": "A true Chinese junk is a great curiosity; the model must have been taken originally from a bread-trough, being broad and square at both ends—when light, (I speak of a large one,) it is full thirty feet from the surface of the water to the tafferel, or the highest part of the poop."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "82543165-ae7f-432b-a1f2-2caa124930ea",
                                "sense_id": "bc921ae0-58b6-3bb2-9da9-4ca8d842f0c3",
                                "text": "Yet we should oftener look over the tafferel of our craft, like curious passengers, and not make the voyage like stupid sailors picking oakum."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
